From: isp <40058476+isprogrammer@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iface-modem-voice: don't match calls with different indexes by number

A waiting call from the same number as the active call (the caller puts
the first call on hold and dials again) was matched with the active call:
the active call object took over the waiting call's state, and the real
active call was reported as an unexpected incoming call and lost.

Apply the same index guard the direction/state match already has.
---
--- a/src/mm-iface-modem-voice.c	2026-11-02 22:07:03.344994147 +0000
+++ b/src/mm-iface-modem-voice.c	2026-11-02 22:07:03.345994148 +0000
@@ -226,9 +226,13 @@
         (!call_info->index || !idx || match_index))
         match_direction_and_state = TRUE;
 
-    /* Match number */
+    /* Match number.
+     * Like direction and state, not when both call info and call have an index
+     * set and they're different: a waiting call from the same number as the
+     * active one (e.g. the caller holds and dials again) is a different call. */
     if (call_info->number && number &&
-        g_strcmp0 (call_info->number, number) == 0)
+        g_strcmp0 (call_info->number, number) == 0 &&
+        (!call_info->index || !idx || match_index))
         match_number = TRUE;
 
     /* Match special terminated event.
